  "notes": "{安堵|あんど} expresses the feeling of relief when worry or anxiety is lifted. It has a somewhat literary or formal tone.\n\nUSAGE:\n- {安堵|あんど}する: to feel relieved (verb)\n- {安堵|あんど}の + noun: relief + noun (attributive)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {安堵|あんど}の{息|いき}をつく: to breathe a sigh of relief\n- {安堵|あんど}の{表情|ひょうじょう}: relieved expression\n- {安堵感|あんどかん}: feeling of relief\n- {安堵|あんど}の{色|いろ}を{浮|う}かべる: to show relief (on one's face)\n\nCONTRAST:\n- ほっとする: to feel relieved (casual, everyday)\n- {安心|あんしん}する: to feel at ease, relieved (neutral)\n- {安堵|あんど}する: to feel relieved (literary, formal)\n\nNOTE:\n{安堵|あんど} is often used in written Japanese, news, and formal speech rather than casual conversation.",
